---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="About, Jeff Mills"
  description="Principal-level front-end engineer with 20+ years building accessible, long-lived web platforms and design systems in regulated environments. Open to work that helps people who need it."
>
  <h1 class="page-title">about</h1>

  <hr class="jm-rule" />

  <div class="about-prose">
    <p>
      I'm Jeff, a Principal Front-End Engineer. I've been building for the
      web for 20+ years, first at Philadelphia agencies and then at Vanguard.
      I look at the world through a UI lens. If I press Enter on a button and
      the wrong thing closes, I notice.
    </p>

    <p>
      At Vanguard I built the design system that 11 product teams and the
      main advisor portal run on. I'm the technical lead for it. I also set the long-term technical
      direction for Expert Insights, Vanguard's AI portfolio analysis tool,
      which went to pilot in April 2026. The design system team started as just me. It's
      five engineers now, and I hired them.
    </p>

    <p>
      The agency years made me fast. Vanguard taught me to build for scale,
      and to ship when compliance review, accessibility requirements, and a
      long line of stakeholders are part of every release. I like that kind
      of work a lot. The constraints are where most of the real engineering
      is.
    </p>

    <p>
      The best decision I made there was the oldest one. In 2018 I worked out
      how to compile Vue components into plain Web Components so any team
      could use them. That is still holding up the system eight years later,
      through three framework generations, and it became the base for
      generative-UI work none of us had imagined.
    </p>

    <p>
      I work as a hands-on technical lead. I write code next to the engineers
      I work with and pair through the hard parts. Lately a lot of that is
      AI-assisted coding with Claude: the design system's first CI test
      gates, tests that run every component in a real browser, and a
      generative-UI pipeline that builds pages from our components and live
      data.
    </p>

    <p>
      What I want next is front-end work for people who really need it. Twenty years in,
      impact per line of code starts to matter more. A benefits form that
      works on a cheap phone changes more lives than another advisor
      dashboard.
    </p>
    <p class="about-locale">
      <span class="jm-badge">&gt;</span>Based in the Philadelphia area.
    </p>
  </div>

  <hr class="jm-rule" />

  <p class="about-cta">
    Open to front-end roles where the work helps people who need it. Let me know if you want to talk through any of this: <a href="mailto:jeffy9@gmail.com">say hello</a>
    &middot; <a href="/resume">read resume</a>
    &middot; <a href="https://github.com/k0bura">github.com/k0bura</a>
  </p>
</Base>

